+# Generator fix report: evaluator-rubric.md defects
+
+Base: `759b007` (evaluated feature `f53fa54`). `evaluator-rubric.md` and `rubric-template.md` were not edited.
+
+## What changed
+
+| # | Defect | Fix | Where |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| 1 | Failed question silently lost | `askError` (one entry) is now `askErrors: AskError[]`. A new ask no longer clears failures. Each failure keeps its question until **that** entry is retried (it then becomes the pending turn) or dismissed. Clear still empties the list. | `App.tsx`, `conversation-format.ts` (`addAskError`/`removeAskError`, unit-tested), `ConversationView.tsx` |
+| 2 | Ghost `DocumentDetail` for a deleted cited document | `handleOpenCitation` now always confirms through `documents.get(id)` and does not trust the cached list. If the document is missing it returns false (so the "no longer available" notice shows), closes the detail if that document was open, and refreshes the stale list. | `App.tsx` |
+| 3 | Focus falls to `<body>` after confirming Clear | On success, focus moves to the conversation heading (`h2`, `tabIndex=-1`). On failure, it moves back to the Clear button. | `ConversationView.tsx` |
+| 4 | No recovery from an unreadable history at startup | Clear is enabled in the `error` load state. The confirmation reads "Replace the unreadable conversation history with an empty one?", and the error panel points to Clear. Confirming writes `[]` through the existing `qa:clear-history` and reloads. | `ConversationView.tsx` |
+| 5 | Escape doesn't cancel the Clear confirmation | `onKeyDown` on the confirm group: Escape calls `cancelClear` (focus goes back to Clear). | `ConversationView.tsx` |
+| 6 | 18 forward Tabs to reach the newest citations | A "Jump to latest answer" skip button sits right after Ask. It is visually hidden until focused and moves focus to the newest exchange (`#latest-exchange`, `tabIndex=-1`). There is also an Alt+ArrowUp shortcut in the input, exposed via `aria-keyshortcuts`. Input → Tab, Tab, Enter, Tab reaches the newest citation (4 presses). | `QuestionPanel.tsx`, `ConversationTurns.tsx` |
+| 7 | D-1 recorded outside `sprint-contract.md` | **Not done. Needs the user's decision.** In the earlier session the user told the Generator to leave `sprint-contract.md` unedited, and the rubric makes this edit conditional on the user's permission. D-1 is still documented in `generator/generator-report.md`. | — |
+| 8 | Raw technical error text | Plain wording ("Something went wrong and this question could not be answered. Your question is kept here so you can try it again.") with the raw message inside a closed `<details>` "Technical details" disclosure. | `ConversationTurns.tsx` |
+
+Refactor that came with the fixes: the turn components (`UserTurn`, `CitationList`, `Exchange`, `PendingTurn`, `FailedTurn`) moved from `ConversationView.tsx` (454 → 237 lines) into `ConversationTurns.tsx`. There is no service, main, preload or IPC change, and the `qa-history.json` schema is unchanged.
+
+## Verification
+
+- `npm run check`: exit 0. `npm run build`: OK. `bash scripts/check-architecture.sh`: PASS. `npx vitest run`: 9/9 (2 new tests for the failure list).
+- Runtime, built app, isolated `--user-data-dir`, real CDP input events (`scripts/fixes.mjs`, `scripts/cdp.mjs`):
+  - Phase A (fresh data dir), `results-a.json`: **14/14 PASS**, covering defects 1, 8, 2, 6, 5 and 3.
+  - Phase B (app started on a corrupted `qa-history.json`), `results-b.json`: **4/4 PASS**, covering defect 4: Clear enabled → confirm → file is `[]` → empty state → a new ask persists.
+  - No exceptions or console errors in either phase (only Electron's pre-existing dev CSP warning).
+  - Logs: `run-a.log`, `run-b.log`. Screenshots: `01`–`09`.
+- Driver note: the first phase-B run timed out because the driver typed into the input in the same frame that the defect-3 fix moved focus to the heading. The driver now waits for that focus move. This was a test race, not an app bug.
+
+## Remaining risks
+
+- Defect 7 is open until the user decides (see above).
+- Failed questions are kept only in renderer memory, as before. They don't survive a restart, by design, because the history schema is unchanged.
+- Out of scope, seen during the run: after a document is deleted, new answers can still cite its chunks as "Unknown Document" (the index isn't purged on delete; service behaviour, pre-existing).
+- Screen-reader announcement is still unverified (DOM roles only).
